\DOC MEMSAFE_ARITH_TAC

\TYPE {MEMSAFE_ARITH_TAC : tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Closes an arithmetic goal by linear arithmetic reasoning over the arithmetic
assumptions of the goal.

\DESCRIBE
Takes no arguments. Applied to a goal {A ?- t} whose conclusion is an
arithmetic proposition over the naturals (possibly built up with disjunction,
conjunction, or chained implications), it selects the arithmetic facts among
the assumptions {A}, discharges them as antecedents of {t}, and proves the
resulting implication with an arithmetic decision procedure:
{
           A ?- t
     =====================  MEMSAFE_ARITH_TAC
}
\noindent Assumptions that are not arithmetic — memory reads, machine-state
relations, list and bit-level facts, quantified statements — are ignored rather
than used.

\FAILURE
Fails when the discharged arithmetic assumptions do not suffice for the
decision procedure to establish the conclusion; in the observed traces this
occurs when the conclusion mentions quantities for which {A} supplies no usable
numeric bound, so that no linear contradiction is found, including conclusions
involving non-linear or opaque subterms. The failure is reported from the
underlying arithmetic rule the tactic invokes.

\COMMENTS
In the observed traces it only ever closes the goal or fails; no trace shows it
transforming a goal.

\ENDDOC
